&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the job&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Twilio is seeking an experienced and dynamic Director to spearhead our Carrier Relations team across Latin America. This role is pivotal in ensuring seamless communication services, driving a localized supply strategy, and fostering strategic partnerships with regional carriers. Working closely with cross-functional partners—such as Sales, Product, Commercial Legal, Regulatory— you will align market demand with local carrier capabilities to power Twilio’s growth in the region. The ideal candidate brings a robust background in telecommunications, deep expertise in LATAM regulatory environments, and a track record of building high-performing teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you’ll:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team Leadership:&lt;/strong&gt; Lead and mentor a team of carrier relations specialists across LATAM, fostering a collaborative, high-performance, and region-aware culture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sales Alignment &amp;amp; Demand Strategy:&lt;/strong&gt; Partner closely with Sales and Product teams to analyze market trends, understand customer demand, and co-develop country-specific supply strategies tailored to individual LATAM markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Carrier/Supply Partnerships &amp;amp; Negotiation:&lt;/strong&gt; Develop and maintain strong, strategic relationships with regional and local carriers and other suppliers to secure cost-effective solutions, expand coverage, and optimize service delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Regulatory &amp;amp; Market Intelligence:&lt;/strong&gt; Navigate complex local telecommunications regulations and upcoming policy changes to proactively adapt Twilio&#39;s supply strategy and maintain strict compliance across all LATAM territories.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Performance &amp;amp; KPI Management:&lt;/strong&gt; Implement and monitor localized KPIs to assess supplier performance, route quality, and cost efficiency in alignment with regional business goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operational Execution:&lt;/strong&gt; Act as an escalation point to resolve regional carrier/supplier service issues, minimizing operational disruption and maintaining high service reliability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
