&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the job&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Product Manager you will help scale Twilio’s core identity product delivering secure, developer-first identity experiences. You’ll build products that power authentication, authorization, and emerging agentic and non-human identity use cases. You’ll partner closely with product and engineering leadership to design and deliver high-impact customer-facing features. This is a rare chance to operate like a startup within Twilio: you’ll work in a high-ownership environment with startup speed, backed by Twilio’s reach and scale.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you’ll:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design product capabilities for Identity platform on Twilio—building new products that help our customers’ secure their applications for both agentic and human identity use cases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product and Engineering leadership to set direction, translate customer needs into product capabilities, and build the roadmap to deliver on these capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate across Twilio teams to align on product direction and unblock cross-team initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operate with deep product ownership: author PRFAQs, product requirement docs, collaborate closely with engineering and design to bring these ideas to life, and enable our go-to-market teams to help our customs solve their challenges leveraging our products.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build in ambiguity—break down complex problems, make pragmatic tradeoffs, and design developer experiences that delight our customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be the voice of the customer in every conversation and decision, and ensure we build world class products that our customers value.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
