&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the job&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position is needed to advance the quality, reliability, and strategic value of Twilio’s Go-To-Market (GTM) data by designing and maintaining robust business data models to enable trusted sales analytics, reporting, data science, &amp;amp; AI capabilities. The Staff, Business Intelligence Engineer will play a mission-critical role in our evolution from traditional BI to AI, ensuring data consistency and empowering data-driven decision-making.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you’ll perform:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;​​&lt;strong&gt;Data Analysis and Interpretation: &lt;/strong&gt;Utilize advanced analytical techniques to analyze large datasets, extract meaningful insights, and provide actionable recommendations to enhance revenue operations efficiency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data Monitoring:&lt;/strong&gt; Develop and maintain automated data reconciliation and quality checks to proactively identify and resolve discrepancies, ensuring accuracy and consistency of critical reports and dashboards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data Visualization:&lt;/strong&gt; Create compelling visualizations to effectively communicate complex data insights, making information accessible and actionable for a diverse audience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data Modeling: &lt;/strong&gt;Build and maintain data models to support GTM, helping the organization make informed strategic decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data Automation (BI-as-Code): Drive the automation of our business intelligence ecosystem by treating dashboards and semantic layers as code. You will leverage Git, automated testing frameworks, and CI/CD pipelines to ensure our data infrastructure is reproducible, version-controlled, and highly scalable&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Collaboration:&lt;/strong&gt; Work closely with various teams, including Sales, Marketing, Finance, and Product, to understand business requirements and provide analytical support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Continuous Improvement:&lt;/strong&gt; Identify opportunities to enhance data quality, reporting processes, and analytics tools to drive continuous improvement in data analysis capabilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Twilio values diverse experiences from all kinds of industries, and we encourage everyone who meets the required qualifications to apply. If your career is just starting or hasn&#39;t followed a traditional path, don&#39;t let that stop you from considering Twilio. We are always looking for people who will bring something new to the table!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;*Required:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum 8 years of professional experience in business intelligence, analytics engineering, data engineering, or a related discipline, with a preference for direct experience supporting GTM or sales analytics in a SaaS environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with business intelligence platforms such as Tableau, particularly in the context of executive reporting and sales analytics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced expertise in SQL and hands-on experience designing data models&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to partner with cross-functional stakeholders to codify, document, and reconcile critical business metrics, ensuring company-wide data alignment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of implementing robust data quality and testing frameworks, including expertise with CI/CD and data observability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical communication and mentorship skills, with the ability to convey complex concepts to a range of audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Desired:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in a quantitative discipline (e.g., Computer Science, Engineering, Mathematics, Economics).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A software engineering mindset applied to data - understanding code reviews, automated testing, and environment separation (Dev/Staging/Prod)&lt;/li&gt;
